  "proof": [
    "Home reads bounded authenticated envelope metadata and retains addressability. LocalResumeCoordinator reads the selected envelope; GameShellRouter recognizes Whodunit PassAndPlay capability; ResumeLocal maps to actual WhodunitGameFlow independent of stale mode metadata. No generic infrastructure change or Solo mode capability is needed.",
    "Original source branch explicitly deleted a loaded Solo record before decoding its private payload and converted successful deletion to NotFound. Original HEAD branch436-441 and unchanged red cycle loader hash b5b57dfe7675a0f85e299719f5161d9e50d75e6c0f1c25cfb72379e7b032ec36 confirm the deterministic cause.",
    "Current source deletes only the obsolete Solo special-case and constant, then reuses the existing unsupported-mode guard before content identity construction or snapshotCodec.decode. Solo/other unsupported modes return CorruptedData with no store mutation. Game/session/engine guards still run first; valid PassAndPlay follows unchanged codec/case validation.",
    "load cancellation propagates at snapshotStore.load outside the try; inner CancellationException catch still rethrows. No new catch converts cancellation or platform storage failures to empty success. Test now injects actual load cancellation, not a removed deletion site.",
    "WhodunitGameFlow prioritizes resumed Failure and renders RecoveryErrorScreen, not SessionDrivenFlow or ConfiguredFlow. Retry increments generation and reloads; Back leaves without deletion. Therefore no canonical reducer, automatic AssignRoles or SerializedSnapshotWriter is instantiated for Solo recovery. Explicit Discard removes only selected id; failure leaves UI/actions available and reports failure.",
    "Regression uses intentionally undecodable Solo payload atop the real envelope store. Exact GameSnapshot equality independently verified to compare every field plus payload.contentEquals; save/delete call counts both remain zero and listUnfinished still contains the id. This establishes logical payload/envelope preservation, not platform encryption or disk-byte durability.",
    "English/Arabic actual recovery UI tests run at320x640dp/1.3fontscale; each checks explanatory text and record equality after initial display, Retry, Back, remount, then invokes accessible Discard. Only selected record disappears, unrelated record remains, exactly1delete and0save. Root-authored Solo fixture correctly expects loader Failure rather than earlier compatible-mode fixture Success.",
    "All17 red cases execute:3 expected failures assert CorruptedData but see NotFound;14 pass including cancellation and prior incompatible/identityless flows. The2 EN/AR red cases fail in Fixture.prepare before Compose, so this is a loader red witness, not a claim of red UI traversal.",
    "Green27cases across5classes all execute and pass without failures/errors/skips; includes3 former red cases, load cancellation,6 actual UI recovery cases, exact-content compatibility, and the story deterministic trace. Red→green source manifests differ only in loader and2documentation files; both test sources are identical across the witness/repair cycles, so assertions were not weakened.",
    "Updated current docs explicitly state retired/unsupported modes are kept until explicit discard and not converted to PassAndPlay. Other game/protocol/seed/content/snapshot-schema behavior is untouched by this patch."
  ],
  "counter_evidence": [
    "Old tests and comments demanded Solo auto-deletion; current owner preservation policy has no Solo exemption, so those tests encoded superseded product behavior, not a reason to retain destructive reads.",
    "Malformed payload cannot itself establish guard ordering because generic decode errors also map to CorruptedData; ordering is proven directly by current source before451, with test ensuring no mutation/decoder-dependent success.",
    "GameSnapshot is a data class with custom ByteArray equality, not default referential ByteArray equality; no false-green or unnecessary fixture rewrite here.",
    "InMemorySnapshotStore returns same GameSnapshot objects; actual mutation under test would have to call save/delete or alter mutable payload. Source contains no such write before rejection. FileBackedSnapshotStore reconstruction test separately decodes envelope bytes and checks equality.",
    "Valid legacy decode support remains separate from permission to launch a game with absent content identity. No new format migration, protocol change, role/seed exposure, room/history behavior or Mafia change is introduced.",
    "Recovery retry case producer subtlety was separately registered previously; not silently fixed or decided in this preservation patch."
  ],
